{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recorder-events-017-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/SeedEventTests.cs","line":629,"method":"EmitSeedEvents_EmptyAllEngineKeys_NoSentinels","category":"T2","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/PartStateSeeder.cs:745; emit the EngineShutdown sentinel unconditionally before the allEngineKeys loop -> red; the same change also reds EmitSeedEvents_EmptySets_ReturnsZeroEvents.","what_it_asserts":"With all tracking sets empty, EmitSeedEvents produces no EngineShutdown events.","why_weak":"The input is the same all-empty PartTrackingSets as EmitSeedEvents_EmptySets_ReturnsZeroEvents, which already asserts the whole result list is empty plus the summary log line. No production change reds this test without also redding that one, and the dead-engine loop it names can never run on this input.","proposed_action":"Delete it, or strengthen it into a real negative for the #298 loop (allEngineKeys populated with keys that are all in activeEngineKeys is already covered by EmitSeedEvents_AllEnginesActive_NoShutdownSentinels).","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
